<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surat is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, a major commercial centre under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. In 1664 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> raided it. Accounts of the Maratha Empire treat the raid as a demonstration of Maratha power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surat.jpg" alt="Surat" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rahul Bhadane · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bharthana_Althan_area.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
